                <pb facs="0271" n="[197]" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg197"/>

                <head>[Memorandum.]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-11-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 19, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>A large order for insulated telegraphic wire has been given by the confederates
                    to Silvee &amp; Co., London, with the intention of using it to explode
                    torpedoes, or vessels filled with powder, beneath federal ships-of-war. The
                    order is a very large one, and our agents should endeavor to prevent it arriving
                    in a southern port.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
